"""Evidence-grounded interview content; no experiment execution."""
# Each tuple: category, question, short answer, deeper answer, key facts, mistake to avoid.
QUESTIONS = [
('1. Problem understanding','What are you predicting?','One of four construction-era classes for each Landsat pixel.','The labels summarize building ages within mixed 30 m pixels. We are not estimating an exact year for every individual roof. The application motivation is incomplete urban records, but our evidence is a supplied two-city classification benchmark, not a deployed urban-planning system.','Four classes; Madrid source, Amsterdam target. [S01,S03]','Calling a pixel an independent building or claiming exact-year prediction.'),
('1. Problem understanding','What makes this transfer learning rather than ordinary classification?','Source-supervised information must influence target predictions.','In EXP-010, Madrid supplies feature relevance and class offsets. In ASTRA/Coordinate_RF, a Madrid-trained aligned contextual prior contributes to target probabilities. The reference few-shot prototypes largely use target support means; a source RF trained elsewhere in the notebook does not automatically make that prototype path supervised transfer.','EXP-010: source ranking/geometry; current model: contextual prior. [S04,S05,S12]','Saying the baseline target-only prototype directly consumes the fitted RF.'),
('1. Problem understanding','What would success outside this benchmark require?','A specified deployment information contract and genuinely unseen geographic evaluation.','We would need to know whether full unlabelled target features and coordinates are available, fix the label-dependent preprocessing membership path, and evaluate a locked method on an untouched city or organizer split. Current exact replays establish internal reproducibility, not those missing deployment conditions.','One target city; pool-bound current artifact. [S12-S16]','Equating a higher internal F1 with city-portable deployment.'),
('2. Dataset','How many observations do you have?','76,263 Madrid and 25,992 Amsterdam pixel vectors, each with 60 input columns.','Raw data are annual records: about 3.17 million Madrid and 1.06 million Amsterdam pixel-year rows. Aggregation creates one vector per pixel. Counting annual rows as independent training examples would exaggerate the effective spatial sample size; neighboring pixels also remain correlated.','76,263 / 25,992 pixels; observed 1984-2025, 42 years. [S02,S03]','Saying millions of independent buildings or using the earlier 2024 end year as a verified current data fact.'),
('2. Dataset','Are the classes balanced and identical between cities?','No: counts are unequal, and the oldest-era boundary differs by city.','Amsterdam counts are 7,568, 8,802, 6,745 and 2,877. Both cities share later cutpoints, but Madrid uses 1960 for its early boundary and Amsterdam 1945. Balanced support sampling and class-balanced forests help define the experiment; they do not make the naturally imbalanced query distribution balanced.','Amsterdam classes 1-4: 7568/8802/6745/2877. [S03]','Saying Class 1 is largest or that balanced support means balanced queries.'),
('2. Dataset','Are your labels exact ground truth for each building?','They are supplied pixel-level age summaries and can represent mixed buildings.','A pixel may contain buildings from several periods plus non-building surfaces. The weighted construction-year label is a useful benchmark target, but it does not identify every roof or quantify label uncertainty. We have not measured a Bayes-error ceiling or verified parcel-disjoint evaluation.','30 m pixels; building/parcel IDs unavailable for that audit. [S01,S10]','Claiming a measured performance ceiling or perfectly noise-free labels.'),
('3. Preprocessing','What transforms raw observations into the model inputs?','QA screening, annual gap filling, spectral/temporal summaries and Madrid-fitted scaling.','The reference selects valid observations, filters high-blue haze, interpolates missing years, computes indices and temporal summaries, then standardizes with source statistics. The accepted local artifact uses a documented minimal scaler shim. The current local RF then restores raw units for its own pool-based covariance transform; preprocessing and model whitening are different stages.','60 ordered features; accepted preprocessing hash begins 51f11bc9. [S03,S14]','Presenting the minimal scaler as proven identical to every sklearn API/version.'),
('3. Preprocessing','Why is label-dependent feature construction a concern?','It prevents claiming a clean raw-data path for hidden-label deployment.','The reference feature builder filters/groups using age-class metadata even though the numerical class is not one of the 60 model features. Thus the feature values and benchmark membership path are not a certified generic hidden-test pipeline. A separate label-free 94-feature branch existed but was rejected and is not silently substituted into the frozen method.','Current inference features exclude age_class; raw builder membership remains label-dependent. [S03,S04]','Answering that everything is leakage-free simply because the RF feature list excludes the target column.'),
('3. Preprocessing','Was your source CV preprocessing fold-safe?','No; the reference scaler was fitted before Madrid CV.','The source reference result must carry that limitation. In an unbiased future source-CV design, preprocessing should be fitted inside each training fold. We did not repair or rerun that baseline in preparation, and the current target paired evaluation should not be mislabelled as corrected source CV.','Reference Madrid CV 0.6281 ±0.0043; pre-CV scaler. [S03]','Claiming independent source CV with fold-local preprocessing.'),
('4. Random Forest','What is a Random Forest and why can it help here?','An ensemble of decision trees captures nonlinear interactions in tabular features.','Trees partition feature space through threshold splits; bootstrap samples and feature subsampling diversify the trees. Averaging probabilities can reduce individual-tree variance. This is well suited to structured spectral summaries, but a forest is not immune to small-support overfitting, geographic shortcuts or source-target shift.','Current local RF: 200 trees, balanced weights, leaf 1, sqrt features. [S12,S14]','Saying forests cannot overfit or do not need validation.'),
('4. Random Forest','Are the source and target forests the same model?','No; distinguish the historical source-ranking forest from the current source-prior and local forests.','EXP-010 uses a 500-tree Madrid RF to derive importance summaries, then target prototypes. ASTRA/Coordinate_RF fit two successive 200-tree source-prior forests with leaf 2 and a separate 200-tree local target-support forest with leaf 1. The current prior is cached; episode adaptation fits the local head.','500 source-ranking trees versus current 200-tree source/local forests. [S05,S14]','Claiming EXP-010 fits a local RF or Coordinate_RF uses the 500-tree ranking forest as its local head.'),
('4. Random Forest','Why is the forest seed not enough to guarantee identical predictions?','Inputs, ordering, versions and floating-point aggregation also matter.','Historical v2 replays exposed one-prediction differences near machine-epsilon probability ties in some arrays. Stable serial aggregation was introduced before the final recipe lock. Exact input/state hashes and prediction-array checks are more convincing than a seed alone, and do not promise every-platform equivalence.','Seed 42; historical ties about 5.55e-17. [S11,S15]','Concluding fixed random_state guarantees bit equality on any machine.'),
('5. Transfer learning','What exactly transfers in EXP-010?','Madrid-supervised feature relevance and relative class geometry.','The selected source-ranked features are weighted by square-root importance. Source class means are expressed as offsets from the source overall mean and recentered on target support. A budget-dependent mixture stabilizes target class prototypes at five shots; above five the representation still transfers even though prototype shrinkage is zero.','k=30/lambda=.6 at 5; k=45/lambda=0 otherwise. [S05]','Saying no transfer remains when lambda is zero.'),
('5. Transfer learning','How does the current source prior adapt without target truth?','It aligns source statistics to unlabelled target features and uses model-generated pseudo-labels.','A globally aligned source forest predicts target pseudo-classes. Source class clouds are aligned once more to corresponding pseudo-labelled target groups before a second forest supplies probabilities. Those guesses may be wrong, so this is not equivalent to obtaining extra labelled target examples or proving that conditional class distributions match.','120 contextual inputs; one conditional alignment iteration. [S12,S14]','Calling pseudo-labels true target labels or guaranteed correct.'),
('5. Transfer learning','Why not use the source model unchanged?','Local zero-shot performance showed substantial source-target mismatch.','The measured local source RF scores about 0.4433 zero-shot, while even target-support prototype adaptation helps. That motivates adaptation but is not the fair primary comparator for transfer benefit: our method must be compared with alternatives receiving the same support labels and query sets.','Local zero-shot 0.4433; organizer-saved 0.3427 is a separate record. [S03,S05]','Claiming the full difference from zero-shot measures transfer improvement.'),
('6. Few-shot setup','What is an episode?','One support selection and its held-out eligible query set.','In the current run, each class supplies a random ordered support prefix; all models receive identical support and query rows for that budget/trial. The query excludes the fixed development bank and current support. The same city and many query pixels are reused across episodes, so episodes measure support-sampling variability rather than independent-city variability.','200 trials × five budgets = 1,000 paired episodes. [S12]','Calling each episode a new dataset or city.'),
('6. Few-shot setup','How many target labels does the current method use?','An episode uses 4b support labels, plus a separately disclosed 800-label research-development bank.','The model recipe was selected using the fixed development bank. The final episode model receives only its current support labels for local fitting, while full-pool features/coordinates enter transductive operations. It would be misleading to call the entire research project a 20-label exercise because one evaluated episode has five shots/class.','5/class=20; 200/class=800; separate development bank=800. [S12]','Hiding development supervision behind the episode budget.'),
('6. Few-shot setup','Are budgets nested and trials independent?','Budgets are nested within a trial; query populations overlap heavily across trials.','One per-class permutation supplies prefixes for the current five budgets, reducing irrelevant differences between learning-curve points. This creates correlation between budgets. Conditional episode bootstrap can describe the saved support-draw regime but is not a pixel-independent or city-level resampling procedure. Competitor headline budgets followed a different RNG convention.','Final seed 20260910; nested prefixes. [S10,S12,S14]','Treating all 1,000 episode scores as independent observations in a pooled test.'),
('7. Feature selection','How were EXP-010 features selected?','By Madrid-supervised RF importance, retaining the frozen top-k dimensions.','The ranking uses source labels, not final-query labels. Square-root weighting turns importance into a multiplier of squared Euclidean distance. The choice of k/lambda was a historical development decision, so source-only ranking does not make the entire selection process independent of target research feedback.','Top 30 at 5, top 45 at 25-200. [S05]','Confusing source-only ranking with no target-side model selection ever.'),
('7. Feature selection','Why did 94 engineered features not win?','The saved comparison showed little selection benefit and worse audit performance at most budgets.','Additional seasonal, coverage and temporal information was plausible and a label-free builder was useful. However, the measured feature comparison did not support adoption. More noisy or redundant dimensions may worsen few-shot estimates, but the exact causal reason was not isolated; the negative result is narrower than all feature engineering being useless.','About +.0001 selection mean; 8/25 audit wins. [S04]','Claiming dilution was proved or all extra features are bad.'),
('7. Feature selection','Can RF importance tell us which original spectral band caused the gain?','Not from the current whitened-axis impurity ranking alone.','The local RF uses covariance-transformed axes that mix raw inputs. Its impurity importances indicate split usage in that representation and can favor some variable types. Coordinates can be separately identified as appended columns, but even their importance is descriptive, not causal or a validated feature-ablation effect.','Current local dimensions: 60 whitened axes +2 coordinates. [S14]','Relabelling a whitened axis as raw NIR importance or calling importance causal attribution.'),
('8. ASTRA-AGF','Explain adaptive geometry without equations.','It uses target feature correlations but trusts a simpler geometry when support is tiny.','Full unlabelled target covariance describes how features vary together. Budget-dependent shrinkage reduces off-diagonal covariance at small support counts, then permits more decorrelation as support increases. That transformed representation feeds a support-trained RF; it is not just a different Euclidean prototype or a learned neural embedding.','rho=min(1,60/(4b)); 60 local inputs. [S11,S14]','Saying rho is newly tuned per final query set.'),
('8. ASTRA-AGF','What does the spatial graph do?','It averages neighboring predicted probabilities with fixed Gaussian weights.','After source/local blending, self plus eight nearest lattice neighbors contribute one smoothing step. No ground-truth query labels or support-truth clamping are used. Support predictions are still influenced by support fitting, so prediction-only smoothing can benefit from spatial adjacency; it does not establish independent samples.','Nine neighbors including self; sigma=1 key unit; one pass. [S14]','Saying no truth anchors means no spatial dependence or shortcut benefit.'),
('8. ASTRA-AGF','Which ASTRA score should we quote?','Use 0.733037 as the matched 200-shot control for current Coordinate_RF comparisons.','Historical ASTRA 0.735239 ±0.005406 comes from its 100-trial seed-104729 regime, without the later development-query exclusion. It remains valid historical evidence but is not the paired control for Coordinate_RF 0.749299. A third value, 0.737388, belongs to the earlier competitor-convention comparison.','Historical .735239; current matched .733037; same-20 comparison .737388. [S10-S12]','Mixing means from different protocols because the model name is the same.'),
('9. Coordinate-RF','What changed relative to ASTRA?','Two full-pool-standardized coordinate columns were appended to the local RF inputs.','The 60 whitened local features become 62. The 120-feature contextual source prior, source blending schedule, covariance rule, RF settings and Gaussian graph remain unchanged. This is a development-selected variant of the existing recipe, not a new raw spectral representation or a different classifier.','Local 62; source context 120; config {coord: true}. [S12,S14]','Claiming only Coordinate_RF uses space; ASTRA already uses spatial context and smoothing.'),
('9. Coordinate-RF','Why is Coordinate_RF the current incumbent?','It was selected and locked on the designated development protocol before final-query scoring.','Its 160-shot repeated development-holdout mean improved by about .008034 over ASTRA with 15/20 wins and passed the stated development safeguards. Its later random-query gain was not used to retune or reselect it. Incumbent means the packaged research choice in this access regime, not an official organizer promotion.','Lock 2026-09-09 17:50:37 local recorded time; final seed 20260910. [S12]','Saying we chose it because its final 0.749299 was highest.'),
('9. Coordinate-RF','Does the artifact predict arbitrary new cities?','No; it is bound to the supplied ordered target pool and coordinates.','The cached prior, covariance and neighbor structure belong to 25,992 Amsterdam rows. A different or reordered pool violates the input contract. A future new-pool evaluation would need the unchanged source-fitting procedure with appropriate source data and new target features, plus an independently justified evaluation protocol.','25992-row pool; exact feature order and row indices. [S11,S14]','Treating the cached Amsterdam artifact as a generic unseen-city pointwise estimator.'),
('10. Spatial robustness','Why test geographic halves?','Random-pixel sampling may benefit from nearby, similar locations and hide extrapolation difficulty.','A buffered opposite-half query tests a harder geography under the same transductive access regime. All four directions are reported, not just the favorable side. It is still one city’s diagnostic with limited partitions; building/parcel independence is not established.','200 shots; 10 trials/direction; 10-key buffer. [S13]','Calling four directions four independent cities.'),
('10. Spatial robustness','Does Coordinate_RF improve geographic robustness over ASTRA?','No, not in the reported overall directional comparison.','Its x-half and four-direction means are lower, its y-half mean is nearly equal but lower, and its worst-direction mean is worse. Random-pixel gains coexist with poorer regional extrapolation. This is exactly why we cannot claim it is a universal replacement despite 200/200 high-shot random wins.','Four-direction .694216 vs .696672; worst .644816 vs .658183. [S13]','Omitting ASTRA or quoting only the coordinate variant directions that improved.'),
('10. Spatial robustness','Is the buffer 300 metres and does it prevent all leakage?','The audited contract is ten lattice-key units; it is not a universal leakage guarantee.','Older notes interpret keys as a 30 m lattice, but the latest method/report treats key units as authoritative rather than casually asserting geographic metres. A buffer reduces immediate support adjacency across the split, while full-pool statistics and spatial dependence still exist. It does not identify same-building overlap or prove domain generalization.','10 key units; coordinates must follow the supplied integer lattice. [S10,S13,S14]','Equating a distance buffer with fully independent geographic validation.'),
('11. Validation','How was model selection separated from final evaluation?','The latest candidate was locked using designated support-development labels before final-query scoring.','A fixed 800-label bank supported initial folds, repeated holdouts and development spatial safeguards. Those pixels are excluded from final queries, and final support comes from outside the bank. The inherited ASTRA recipe had earlier audit exposure; the new separation cannot erase its history or create an organizer-hidden population.','Development seed 20260909; final seed 20260910. [S12]','Claiming the whole project has an untouched test set.'),
('11. Validation','What do the paired tests establish?','Conditional evidence for mean support-sampling gains on the stated fixed target population.','The analyses compare Coordinate_RF and controls by identical budget/trial keys, apply paired t and Wilcoxon tests, paired episode-bootstrap confidence intervals and effect sizes. Holm adjusts across 15 comparisons in each test family. These procedures do not measure between-city variation or remove historical selection bias.','200-shot ASTRA gain CI about [.015856,.016669]. [S14]','Interpreting a tiny p-value as proof of generalization to any city.'),
('11. Validation','What was Gate4 E2 good for if it missed the target?','It showed a reproducible small gain without satisfying the predefined practical success rule.','At 25 shots the exact-reconstructed mean gain was .004953 and 10/10 pairs improved, but the required mean gain was .0100. Calling it inconclusive under that rule respects the original criterion; inventing a lower threshold after seeing results would undermine the test.','E2 .603550 vs raw .598598; threshold +.0100. [S08]','Relabelling E2 as successful because its p-value or win count looks favorable.'),
('12. Leakage','Did you use the target test labels?','Current estimators use designated support labels; query truth is for evaluation, but historical research selection exposure is disclosed.','The benchmark sampler uses labels for class-balanced support construction. A separate 800-label bank supports current selection. Historical ASTRA was audit-selected. The current inference API does not receive query truth, yet saying target labels were never used anywhere would be false, and the reference feature-builder deployment issue remains.','800 development labels; 4b episode support labels; historical audit exposure. [S03,S11,S12]','Answering a blanket no without distinguishing fitting, sampling, selection and scoring.'),
('12. Leakage','Is using the entire unlabelled target pool cheating?','It is transductive learning; rule compliance depends on the organizer information contract.','Means, covariance, pseudo-labels and graph structure use unlabelled target features/coordinates, not hidden query truth. This is a different privilege from inductive support-only adaptation. Our open-scope research assumes it, but the latest organizer message specifies deliverables, not permission for full-pool learning.','Full ordered target pool required; permission not confirmed by submission email. [S06,S11,S16]','Claiming coordinates/full-pool use is officially approved without evidence.'),
('12. Leakage','Can neighboring support predictions contaminate query predictions even without explicit labels?','They can transmit support-trained signal; that is spatial dependence, not automatically forbidden query-label use.','The RF is trained on support labels and predicts the full pool. Smoothing averages those probabilities, including predictions at support locations. The absence of explicit truth anchoring narrows the leakage claim, but does not remove adjacency benefits. Whether that is allowed depends on the evaluation regime.','Prediction-only Gaussian averaging; spatial stress reported. [S10,S13,S14]','Saying prediction-only smoothing guarantees unbiased independent-pixel evaluation.'),
('13. Reproducibility','What is the strongest replay evidence?','A fresh-source rebuild matched eight state arrays and 4,000 prediction arrays across 1,000 episodes.','The existing original replay includes both inductive controls and the two RF methods. Later publication independently recalculated saved confusion/F1 records and verified fixed-reference calls. These are clean-process computational checks; they must not be described as a second human team or an independent organizer dataset.','4,000 arrays; 1,000 episodes; no expensive replay rerun in preparation. [S15]','Confusing clean process with independent scientist or independent city.'),
('13. Reproducibility','Can someone reproduce the publication outside this workspace?','The existing extracted-archive test passed five reference predictions and byte-identical rebuilt CSVs.','That ZIP contains the inference state, saved numeric evidence and preprocessed data under a defined allowlist. The organizer fallback ZIP is a different, smaller package and deliberately excludes target-truth data. Reproducible publication evidence is therefore not the same claim as a complete final notebook submission.','Publication ZIP hash starts ed8ff94f; safety ZIP has its own seal. [S15,S16]','Sending the large label-containing publication archive automatically as the minimal organizer deliverable.'),
('13. Reproducibility','What does your safety snapshot actually guarantee?','The 13 intended fallback files and ZIP have verified hashes and write protection; submission completeness remains explicitly unresolved.','We preserved existing EXP-010 presentation/text, reference notebooks and minimal code/state. No final-method notebook was found. Seven background OneNote indexes appeared after sealing and were not deleted; the sealed ZIP excludes them. NTFS deny-write/delete and hashes protect/detect accidental changes, but owner/admin access is not WORM storage.','13 intended files; exact clean ZIP; no invented final notebook. [S16]','Claiming a perfect current-model submission or silently ignoring post-seal directory additions.'),
('14. Competitor comparison','Why is your score higher than the competitor?','The headline numbers use different protocols, so we do not claim that subtraction is a fair paired win.','Our current .749299 excludes the fixed development bank and uses 200 trials/budget. Their locally recorded .7373 used 20 draws, another representation/configuration and earlier selection exposure. We can defend paired gains versus our current ASTRA/EXP-F/EXP-010 controls, not an exact comparison to an unavailable tuned competitor model.','Current .749299; historical competitor claim .7373; not paired. [S10,S12]','Saying we beat their exact best model by the difference of those means.'),
('14. Competitor comparison','Did you copy competitor code or use their data?','No competitor payload is in our model implementation or safety snapshot; historical forensic execution was separate.','Our own audits inspected their method and separately ran a labelled fallback mechanism with supplied data. The later candidate was independently implemented from this repository’s inputs and explicit formulas. Acknowledging mechanism inspiration is more accurate than pretending no comparison was studied. All forensic material remains outside the submission fallback.','Own 60/120/62 representations; competitor tuned config unrecovered. [S10,S12,S16]','Claiming no competitor code was ever executed anywhere in research, or claiming code originality proves conceptual novelty.'),
('14. Competitor comparison','What was their latest update and was it a breakthrough?','Latest locally evidenced update is cf9af6c: distance-weighted smoothing, claimed .7373 at 200 shots.','That update improved the earlier uniform-smoothing .7259 claim. It would be wrong to deny the reported improvement. We found no subsequently demonstrated local breakthrough beyond it, did not fetch new remote history in preparation, and still lack the winning configuration. Near reproduction is not exact winner reconstruction.','cf9af6c, 2026-09-09 14:23:35 +02; .7259 to .7373. [S10]','Turning lack of a newer local record into a claim that the competitor has made no progress anywhere.'),
('15. Why not neural networks?','Why did you not use a neural network as the final model?','The frozen evidence supports the chosen tabular RF recipe; no validated neural-network advantage is recorded.','The local adaptation sets are small and the inputs are structured spectral summaries. A neural model would require additional design, regularization and honest validation. We do not claim to have proved neural networks inferior, and this preparation task cannot authorize an untested neural search.','Local support 20-800 labels; current RF 200 trees. [S12,S14]','Inventing a neural-network experiment or saying neural networks always need millions of labels.'),
('15. Why not neural networks?','Could a pretrained sequence model use the annual satellite series better?','Possibly, but that is untested future work, not our result.','A temporal model could preserve information lost in summaries, yet appropriate pretraining, source/target alignment, label availability and spatial splits would need careful handling. It might improve or worsen robustness. The rejected 94-feature experiment does not establish that all richer temporal representations are useless.','Observed 42-year panels; frozen model consumes 60 summaries. [S03,S04]','Presenting a plausible future architecture as an already demonstrated improvement.'),
('15. Why not neural networks?','Is the RF choice merely because of limited compute?','Compute and reproducibility matter, but the choice is grounded in the actual development evidence.','The frozen RF approach was evaluated under a recorded support-development rule and replayed. We did not run a comprehensive equal-budget deep-learning comparison, so we cannot isolate compute as the causal reason or claim global model-family optimality. Presentation should emphasize evidence over fashionable architecture labels.','Coordinate_RF selected before final scoring; no neural benchmark established. [S12]','Claiming we searched every architecture or selected solely on the final score.'),
('16. Why not another classifier?','Why not XGBoost or boosting?','There is no validated XGBoost result to claim; a histogram-boosted-tree alternative was explored but not selected.','The autonomous report’s BoostedTrees arm uses sklearn HistGradientBoostingClassifier, not XGBoost. Its saved development mean was about .747317 in the reported support-CV comparison and it did not become the locked candidate. That is one operational comparison, not a universal theorem about boosting.','BoostedTrees is sklearn histogram boosting, not XGBoost. [S12]','Renaming the recorded algorithm to a more familiar library or claiming all boosting fails.'),
('16. Why not another classifier?','Why not ExtraTrees if it was competitive?','It was considered in the development selection but Coordinate_RF was the locked choice.','ExtraTrees ranked among the strongest candidates and appears in the lock’s ranked options. The predeclared development rule included mean performance, paired wins, budget stability and geographic safeguards rather than one final-query number. We did not return to selection after seeing Coordinate_RF final results.','Lock ranked Coordinate_RF and ExtraTrees; chosen config coord=true. [S12]','Saying ExtraTrees was obviously poor or discarded because of the final audit.'),
('16. Why not another classifier?','Why not keep the simpler prototype model?','It remains a valuable inductive fallback, but the current richer recipe improves the stated random-pixel task.','EXP-F showed that regularized prototype geometry helps, yet the nonlinear/transductive/spatial branch reached substantially higher internal scores. Its additional information privileges and complexity must be acknowledged. Under unavailable pool/coordinate access, a simpler frozen inductive model may be the more appropriate contract.','Current matched EXP-F .657602; Coordinate_RF .749299 at 200. [S06,S12]','Attributing the whole difference purely to classifier capacity when access and representation also change.'),
('17. Why does performance improve with shots?','Why do more support labels generally help?','They improve estimation of target class structure and stabilize adaptation.','A larger support set samples more target variability, gives more evidence for RF boundaries and reduces sensitivity to a few atypical pixels. The current geometry and source-prior weights also change by fixed formulas with budget. The curve is therefore the performance of a budget-adaptive procedure, not one identical fitted classifier receiving more data.','Coordinate_RF .650253 at 5 to .749299 at 200. [S12]','Claiming an individual episode must improve monotonically whenever support grows.'),
('17. Why does performance improve with shots?','What changes in the source blend as shots increase?','The fixed source weight decreases from .5 at five shots to about .02439 at 200.','The formula is alpha=20/(20+4b). It treats the source prior like a fixed pseudo-count relative to current support. This is a recorded heuristic, not a posterior probability derived from a proven probabilistic model and not a newly optimized lookup table for each final budget.','alpha at 5=.5; at 200=20/820≈.02439. [S14]','Calling alpha a learned confidence score or a calibrated Bayesian posterior.'),
('17. Why does performance improve with shots?','What happens specifically at five shots?','The current model is already much stronger than its inductive controls, but adding local coordinates barely improves ASTRA.','Coordinate_RF .650253 versus ASTRA .649964 yields only .000289 mean gain and 106/200 wins. Its paired gain interval includes zero. Most useful low-shot performance belongs to the inherited prior/geometry/spatial recipe rather than a clear extra benefit from the two local coordinate columns.','Five-shot CI approximately [-.000077,.000667]. [S12,S14]','Using the high-shot coordinate gain to claim coordinates strongly improve every budget.'),
('18. Why does spatial performance vary?','Why can opposite directions give different results?','The two support regions and query regions have different feature/class/geographic distributions.','A low-x support sample may cover relationships that do not hold in high-x queries, and reversing that direction changes both distributions. Coordinates are particularly sensitive to geographic extrapolation. The directional asymmetry is evidence of limited regional transfer, not something to average away without reporting the worst direction.','High-x→low-x coordinate loss vs ASTRA about .028670. [S13]','Treating x/y direction effects as random noise known to vanish with more trials.'),
('18. Why does spatial performance vary?','Are spatial halves a fair matched comparison?','Methods are paired within a direction/trial; random-versus-spatial evaluations have different queries.','All models in the spatial audit share its support and query keys, allowing matched model gains there. The random control shares budget and development exclusions but not query geography or composition, so its mean drop cannot be interpreted as an exact per-pixel causal effect of geography alone.','10 paired trials per direction; four directions. [S13]','Calling random-versus-spatial bars an identical-query experiment.'),
('18. Why does spatial performance vary?','Could you remove coordinates now to fix the spatial weakness?','Not in this frozen preparation task; changing the method would require separate predeclared evaluation.','ASTRA already provides the matched no-local-coordinate control, and its directional mean is slightly stronger. We report that trade-off rather than select a post-audit hybrid or reverse the lock. A future deployment decision must match the intended geography and information contract.','Coordinate_RF remains development-locked; ASTRA historical comparator retained. [S12,S13]','Silently switching models after observing final spatial scores.'),
('19. Why is macro-F1 used?','Why not report accuracy?','Macro F1 gives each class equal weight while balancing precision and recall.','Class 2 dominates the data, so a classifier can look better under accuracy while doing poorly on minority eras. Macro averaging makes each class contribute one quarter of the score. Accuracy, per-class F1 and confusion can remain diagnostics, but must not be substituted for the organizer’s stated metric.','Four-class arithmetic mean of class F1. [S01,S14]','Calling F1 accuracy or reporting only the strongest class.'),
('19. Why is macro-F1 used?','Is a row-normalized confusion diagonal the class F1?','No; it is recall for that true class.','Row normalization divides by the number of true-class appearances. F1 also needs false positives from other rows and uses predicted-class totals as well. A pooled confusion matrix also weights repeated query appearances differently from an unweighted mean of per-episode class F1.','Recall=TP/(TP+FN); F1=2TP/(2TP+FP+FN). [S14]','Labelling a 75% confusion diagonal as 0.75 F1.'),
('19. Why is macro-F1 used?','What does ±0.005716 mean in the headline?','Population SD of the 200 saved episode macro-F1 scores at 200 shots.','It measures spread under the saved support-sampling regime with a fixed forest seed and target population. A confidence interval for the conditional mean is a different quantity; the paired gain bootstrap interval is narrower but also conditional. Neither describes uncertainty over all cities.','ddof=0; 200 episodes/budget. [S12,S14]','Saying 95% of unseen-city scores must fall within mean ±SD.'),
('20. What would you do with more time?','What is the highest-priority next action?','Close the organizer-deliverable gap and verify the permitted inference information contract.','The strongest research result already has publication/replay evidence, but the existing presentation is historical EXP-010 and no final-method notebook was found. Before another discovery sprint, independently prepare a correct final notebook/deck outside the frozen snapshot, clarify full-pool access, and verify the exact organizer-facing package.','Email known; final-method notebook absent; snapshot remains frozen. [S16]','Promising more optimization before a runnable, consistent required submission exists.'),
('20. What would you do with more time?','What scientific validation would matter most?','A genuinely untouched city or organizer-held-out geographic evaluation under predeclared rules.','We would preserve current choices, define access to target covariates/coordinates, avoid post-hoc direction selection, and report failures as well as gains. More support draws on the same city would strengthen sampling precision but not answer the biggest deployment/generalization question.','Current target population is Amsterdam only. [S12-S14]','Saying 10,000 more random episodes would create independent-city evidence.'),
('20. What would you do with more time?','Would you pursue calibration or a new label-free feature pipeline?','Those are reasonable future engineering studies, not completed improvements.','The current calibration figure is diagnostic, not a fitted calibrator. The accepted feature pipeline also needs a hidden-label-safe membership path. Any revised preprocessing or calibration changes predictions and must be separately developed and evaluated; it must not silently replace the frozen model or inherit its score.','No calibration fitted; label-free v2 branch was rejected for the headline. [S03,S04,S14]','Claiming calibration or deployment preprocessing is already solved because a figure or rejected branch exists.'),
('21. What is the biggest weakness?','What is the biggest scientific weakness?','External validity: one historically explored target city with spatially dependent pixels.','There is no organizer-held-out new population, and development labels plus historical audit exposure constrain generalization claims. The geographic audit shows the current coordinate addition is not uniformly better. Exact reproducibility is valuable, but it cannot replace data independence.','Spatial mean .694216 vs ASTRA .696672. [S11-S15]','Choosing only a minor runtime issue while omitting the main validity limitation.'),
('21. What is the biggest weakness?','What is the biggest submission risk?','The required final-method notebook is missing and the deck is not current Coordinate_RF.','The safety snapshot truthfully preserves existing EXP-010 presentation/text and reference notebooks, with supporting code/state. It is a protected fallback, not a complete current-model submission. Its clean ZIP is intact; unsealed background OneNote files in the directory are separately reported.','13 intended snapshot files; final-method notebook requirement unresolved. [S16]','Telling organizers a baseline notebook is the notebook for 0.749299.'),
('21. What is the biggest weakness?','What remains uncertain about historical provenance?','Baseline discrepancy causes, exact competitor tuned configuration and some human-review claims remain unresolved.','Early notes sometimes state stronger causes/replication than later evidence permits. We use qualified audits and specific saved runs, not the most confident sentence. The competitor fallback near-matches a missing tuned model but does not reconstruct it; software clean processes do not establish independent-person review.','Accepted data hash 51f11bc9…; competitor overnight_best.json unrecovered. [S03,S10,S15]','Repeating an early causal story or attributing undocumented human work to balance team credit.'),
('22. Strongest evidence the result is real','Why should we believe 0.7493?','It is the mean of a locked 200-shot protocol, backed by saved paired predictions, exact replay and metric reconstruction.','The source/state rebuild and 4,000-array replay support implementation repeatability. Publication reconstructs all confusion/F1 records and excludes development/support from queries. Against matched ASTRA the high-shot gain is .016262 with 200/200 wins. This validates the stated internal result, not independent-city superiority.','0.749299 ±.005716; +.016262; 200/200. [S12,S15]','Answering only with a p-value or presenting 0.7493 as organizer-scored.'),
('22. Strongest evidence the result is real','How do you know it is not just a lucky episode?','The headline averages all 200 saved episodes at that budget, not a chosen best trial.','We preserve the score distribution, paired wins/losses and conditional intervals. The 200-shot improvement appears across every matched ASTRA pair, whereas the five-shot coordinate difference is inconclusive. This makes a one-episode explanation implausible for the stated regime, but does not remove selection history or spatial limitations.','200-shot 200/200; five-shot 106/200. [S12,S14]','Equating consistency across overlapping-query draws with universal generalization.'),
('22. Strongest evidence the result is real','What failure would make you stop claiming the result?','An integrity/prediction mismatch or a violated evaluation contract would invalidate the affected claim until resolved.','We distinguish byte changes, scientific metric reconstruction and organizer-rule compliance. If a replay fails, report and investigate without overwriting the reference; if pool privileges are disallowed, use a separately qualified inductive method rather than relabeling the transductive score. The snapshot/ZIP provide a preserved fallback, not a license to ignore missing deliverables.','Freeze manifests; clean-reference arrays; explicit support/query boundaries. [S07-S16]','Repairing or deleting inconvenient evidence and continuing to claim an unchanged validated result.'),
]
